<h1>Request Loss Runs</h1>

<p>
    The Request Loss Runs utility helps you efficiently request loss history reports (loss runs) from carriers. It groups policies by carrier, generates professional email requests, and provides multiple ways to contact carriers—all from one convenient interface.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Request Loss Runs utility showing: line of business selector, years selector, carrier groups with policies listed, and action buttons (Send Email, Fallback Email, Access Portal, Send All). Show the organized layout with policies grouped by carrier. -->

<h2>What the Request Loss Runs Utility Does</h2>

<p>
    This utility enables you to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Group by carrier</strong> – Automatically organizes policies by carrier for efficient requesting</li>
    <li><strong>Generate email requests</strong> – Creates professional, formatted emails with all policy details</li>
    <li><strong>Multiple contact methods</strong> – Provides email, portal, and fallback options for each carrier</li>
    <li><strong>Bulk operations</strong> – Send requests to all carriers at once with "Send All"</li>
    <li><strong>Line of business filtering</strong> – Focus on specific coverage types (GL, WC, Auto, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>Year selection</strong> – Specify how many years of loss history you need</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual diagram showing the loss run request workflow: 1) Select line of business and years, 2) Policies grouped by carrier, 3) Choose contact method, 4) Send request, 5) Track sent requests. Use icons and arrows. -->

<h2>Using the Request Loss Runs Utility</h2>

<p>
    To request loss runs:
</p>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Select line of business</strong> – Choose the coverage type you need loss runs for:
        <ul>
            <li>General Liability</li>
            <li>Workers' Compensation</li>
            <li>Commercial Auto</li>
            <li>Property</li>
            <li>Or other available lines</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Select number of years</strong> – Choose how many years of loss history you need (typically 3-5 years)</li>
    <li><strong>Review carrier groups</strong> – The utility automatically groups policies by carrier, showing:
        <ul>
            <li>Carrier name</li>
            <li>List of policies for that carrier</li>
            <li>Policy numbers, effective dates, and expiration dates</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Choose contact method</strong> – For each carrier, select how to send the request:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Send Email</strong> – Send directly through Quickfire's email system</li>
            <li><strong>Fallback Email</strong> – Open your default email client with a pre-filled message</li>
            <li><strong>Access Portal</strong> – Open the carrier's online portal (if configured)</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Send requests</strong> – Send individual requests or use "Send All" to request from every carrier at once</li>
</ol>

