<h2>Understanding Carrier Grouping</h2>

<p>
    The utility automatically groups policies by carrier to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Reduce duplicate requests</strong> – All policies from the same carrier are included in one request</li>
    <li><strong>Organize efficiently</strong> – See at a glance which carriers you need to contact</li>
    <li><strong>Include all policies</strong> – Ensures you don't miss any policies when requesting loss runs</li>
    <li><strong>Simplify tracking</strong> – Easier to track which carriers you've contacted</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Each carrier group shows:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Carrier name</strong> – The insurance company</li>
    <li><strong>Policy list</strong> – All policies from that carrier for the selected line of business</li>
    <li><strong>Policy details</strong> – Policy numbers, effective dates, expiration dates</li>
    <li><strong>Contact information</strong> – Email address or portal link for that carrier</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of a carrier group showing: carrier name header, list of policies with details, and action buttons. Show how multiple policies are grouped together under one carrier. -->

<h2>Email Request Options</h2>

<p>
    You have three ways to send email requests:
</p>

<h3>Send Email</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Sends the request directly through Quickfire's email system</li>
    <li>Uses your configured email integration (Microsoft Graph, etc.)</li>
    <li>Email is sent immediately</li>
    <li>Best for carriers with email addresses stored in Quickfire</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fallback Email</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Opens your default email client (Outlook, Gmail, etc.)</li>
    <li>Pre-fills the subject and body with policy information</li>
    <li>You can review and edit before sending</li>
    <li>Useful when you want to customize the message or add attachments</li>
</ul>

<h3>Access Portal</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Opens the carrier's online portal in a new browser tab</li>
    <li>Only available if a portal URL is configured for that carrier</li>
    <li>Useful for carriers that prefer online submissions</li>
    <li>You'll need to complete the request through the portal interface</li>
</ul>

