<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

<h3>No Policies Showing</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Verify that policies exist for the selected line of business</li>
    <li>Check that policies are active or recently expired</li>
    <li>Ensure the client has policies in Quickfire</li>
    <li>Try selecting a different line of business</li>
</ul>

<h3>Carrier Email Not Available</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Some carriers may not have email addresses configured in Quickfire</li>
    <li>Use "Fallback Email" to send through your email client</li>
    <li>Check if the carrier has a portal option available</li>
    <li>You may need to contact the carrier by phone if no email or portal is available</li>
</ul>

<h3>Portal Link Not Working</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Verify that the carrier's portal URL is configured in Quickfire</li>
    <li>Check that the portal URL is still valid (carriers sometimes change their portals)</li>
    <li>Try accessing the portal directly through the carrier's website</li>
</ul>

<h3>Send All Not Working</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Ensure at least some carriers have email addresses configured</li>
    <li>Check your email integration settings</li>
    <li>Review error messages to see which carriers failed</li>
    <li>Try sending to individual carriers to identify the issue</li>
</ul>

